        "text_jhcj9E": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The equinox marks the point in the year when day and night are equal in length &mdash; a threshold between the outward energy of summer and the inward turn of September through November. In Traditional Chinese Medicine, late summer is counted as a fifth season, lasting until this moment.</p><p>It is about slowing down enough to notice the change, and about what makes a home a home: gathering around the table. Every equinox we circle back to the standards that have defined us from day one &mdash; every supplier tested before we approve them, then randomly audited to ensure consistent compliance with the Seatopia Standard, third-party lab tested for nutrition, mercury and microplastics.</p>",
