    "image_with_text_8biLF6": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_e9TytT": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where Autumn Gathers",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_eUghq3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How we imagine autumn gatherings take shape: fire-pit conversation, a dinner for four that stretches deep into the night, a table dined by your favourite seafood and whatever was available at the farmers market that morning.  This season isn’t about filling the calendar, breaking out or hosting big, energetic gatherings. It’s the chance to hone in on a dish you’re trying to perfect, to try something new with a small, forgiving audience, to keep it simple and spectacular.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
