            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_Vat3rC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>September corresponds with Virgo, a sign associated with earth and an attention to detail. These recipes celebrate the fine print of autumnal produce: the rose-like fractals of maitake, the polka-dot russeting of an Asian pear, the black tiger stripes of shrimp, or the dusky skin of grapes.</p><p>There is a distinct concentration to the way we eat once the light starts to shorten. Rushed and excited conversations are swapped out for quiet, focused ones. And the food that goes with it becomes about moments to savour and celebrate inwardly. </p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
